    "title": "Foul play frustrates Orioles in 5-3 loss to Yankees (updated) - NewsBreak",
    "text": "2 hours ago The Orioles didn’t get a call in the seventh inning tonight or catch a break in the eighth. They felt robbed and then were ruined. An apparent go-ahead home run for Pete Alonso was denied to keep the score tied. Cam Sanders loaded the bases on two hit batters and a walk in his first Camden Yards appearance, Yennier Cano entered with two outs, and George Lombard Jr. reached on a chopper up the third base line. Read full article",
